From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: dma: ensure headroom before inserting alignment pad

mt76_insert_hdr_pad() pushes two bytes without checking headroom.  Forwarded
frames can arrive with no spare headroom and trigger skb_under_panic.  Make
the skb writable with the required headroom before inserting the pad.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -671,8 +671,11 @@ mt76_dma_tx_queue_skb(struct mt76_phy *
 	txwi = mt76_get_txwi_ptr(dev, t);
 
 	skb->prev = skb->next = NULL;
-	if (dev->drv->drv_flags & MT_DRV_TX_ALIGNED4_SKBS)
+	if (dev->drv->drv_flags & MT_DRV_TX_ALIGNED4_SKBS) {
+		if (skb_cow_head(skb, 2))
+			goto free;
 		mt76_insert_hdr_pad(skb);
+	}
 
 	len = skb_headlen(skb);
 	addr = dma_map_single(dev->dma_dev, skb->data, len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
